:: Rent Pay Auto
<<effects>>
<<if $bus is "hospital">>
	The rent has already been covered through your HBSC standing order. Bailey has no reason to come after you for it today.
	<br><br>
	It is not a comforting thought, exactly, but it is one less problem to deal with while you are stuck here.
	<br><br>
	<<if crimeSumCurrent() gte 1000>>
		<<link [[Next|Hospital Arrest]]>><<pass 10>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Next|Hospital front]]>><<pass 10>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if $phase is 1>>
		<<endevent>>
		<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
		You see Robin run up to you from around a corner as you exit <<his>> room. "You're okay!" <<He>> tackles you into a hug.
		"Bailey took me away last night and I thought something awful was going to happen," <<he>> says before calming down.
		<br><br>

		You return the embrace before returning to your room.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<<elseif $inRobinsRoom>>
		<<endevent>>
		<<npc "Robin">><<person1>>
		Robin lets out a breath as Bailey leaves empty-handed. "That was less frightening than usual," <<he>> says quietly.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Orphanage]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<<else>>
        You watch Bailey walk away with <<his>> goon.
        <br><br>
        Only once they are out of sight do you let yourself breathe a long sigh. Thanks to the bank, the matter is settled now.
		<br><br>
        <<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<unset $inRobinsRoom>>

:: Orphanage Charity Mod
<<set _charityAmount to random(500, 1000) * 100>>
<<person3>>
Bailey's frown sharpens. "Then it goes through me. I run the place."
<br><br>
The debate circles the same point several times. The <<person1>><<monk>> speaks of alms, duty, and trust.
Bailey speaks of bills, rules, and debt. You can only watch from the edge of the hall,
hemmed in by curious orphans and nervous initiates.
<br><br>
At last, the <<person2>><<monk>> produces a ledger. The temple has written down every donation,
along with a list of things already delivered to the loft kitchen. Bailey reads it in silence, lips thin.
<br><br>
<<person3>>
"Fine," <<he>> says, snapping the ledger shut. "I don't care where the money comes from as long as I get paid."
<br><br>
<<person2>>
Before the temple group leaves, the <<monk>> presses a sealed envelope into your hands.
"For you," <<he>> murmurs. "There was enough to help some of you directly."
<br><br>
<<person3>>
Bailey glances at the envelope, then back at the tin. "Remember your dues," <<he>> says, already counting the rest.
<br><br>
You open the envelope once <<person3>><<hes>> gone. There's
<<income _charityAmount "orphanageCharity">> inside.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Orphanage]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Bedroom Shackle Pick
<<effects>>
<<set _shackleName to $worn.feet.name>>
<<set _shackleRoom to ($location is "alex_cottage") ? "Farm Bedroom" : "Bedroom">>
You sit on the floor with your back against the bed and open the Lockpick Lawyer set beside you.
The lock on your _shackleName looks much simpler than the practice locks that came with the set.
<br><br>
You hold one ankle close and slide a pick into the lock. Keeping the lock turned with the other tool,
you move the pick around inside until one part gives way, then another.
Your legs start to ache from the awkward position, but the lock opens before you need to stop.
<br><br>
<span class="green">The shackle opens around your ankle.</span>
You move to the other leg and open that one much faster now that you know what to do.
<br><br>
You pack the tools away, then push the shackles under the bed with your foot.
<<remove_shackle>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|_shackleRoom]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Widgets Orphanage Misc [widget]
<<widget "baileyGripDemand">>
	/* Shared hand-grip dialogue used wherever Bailey turns aggressive and rent becomes unavoidable (temple, farm, street hunt).
	Reason from setup.inflation. */
	<<set _gripReason to (setup.inflation ? setup.inflation.baileyAggressionReason() : "")>>
	<<if _gripReason isnot "">>
		<<person1>>
		Before you can get a word out, Bailey's hand clamps around your wrist.
		<<switch _gripReason>>
		<<case "loan">>
			"The bank came to me about what you owe them. Your debt's my problem now, which makes it very much yours.
			You're paying. Today."
		<<case "inflation">>
			<<His>> mouth curls into a knowing smirk. "I know exactly what you've been hoarding.
			Don't insult me by pretending you're short. You've got the money, and I'm done waiting for it."
		<<case "both">>
			<<His>> mouth curls into a knowing smirk. "I know what you've been sitting on, and so does the bank you owe.
			Don't waste my time pretending you can't pay. You'll settle up with me right now, every penny."
		<<case "relentless">>
			<<His>> grip tightens. "Don't bother with the excuses. I don't care how little you've got today.
			You'll pay what I ask, and I'll be asking for more each week. That's just how it is now."
		<<default>>
			<<His>> grip tightens. "You've kept me waiting long enough. You're paying, right now."
		<</switch>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "baileyRentFlavour">>
	/* Special demand wording when wealth raises Bailey's rent cap. See setup.inflation.rentDemand. */
	<<set _rentTier to (setup.inflation ? setup.inflation.rentDemandTier() : "")>>
	<<if _rentTier is "jump">>
		<<person1>><<He>> holds your gaze. "I know exactly how much you're really sitting on. <span class="red">I want more.</span>"
		<br><br>
	<<elseif _rentTier is "investment">>
		<<person1>><<He>> looks you over with a smile. "You know, out of everything I've ever gotten my hands on, you've turned out to be my single best investment.
		Don't think I won't keep asking for more. You can afford it, and we both know it."
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "baileyBankDraw">>
	/* Called during rent payment when cash can't cover it but savings can: Bailey marches the player to HBSC and forces a withdrawal. _args[0] = pennies needed out of savings. */
	<<if setup.hbsc and setup.hbsc.ensureState>><<run setup.hbsc.ensureState()>><</if>>
	<<set _bankDraw to Math.min(Math.ceil(_args[0]), ($hbsc and $hbsc.account and Number.isFinite($hbsc.account.deposit) ? $hbsc.account.deposit : 0))>>
	<<if _bankDraw gt 0>>
		<<person1>>
		<<He>> doesn't buy your empty pockets for a second. "The bank, then. <span class="red">You can't run from me by stuffing it in a vault.</span>"
		<<His>> hand closes around your arm, and <<he>> marches you down the street and in through the doors of HBSC.
		<br><br>
		The teller doesn't so much as care; a withdrawal is a withdrawal. By the door a security guard watches you instead, eyes narrowing, plainly deciding you're the trouble here.
		The message lands: settle this, or you're the one who ends up in danger. Bailey, evidently, <<he>> can handle <<himself>>.
		<br><br>
		You have no choice. You draw <<printmoney _bankDraw>> out of your savings.
		<<set $hbsc.account.deposit -= _bankDraw>><<set $money += _bankDraw>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "rentInflationNotice">>
	/* One-time smirk the first time the player's wealth triggers inflation, when Bailey uncaps the rent and starts demanding more. */
	<<if setup.inflation and setup.inflation.rentInflationActive(setup.inflation.baileyWealth()) and not $rentInflationAnnounced>>
		<<set $rentInflationAnnounced to true>>
		<<person1>>
		<<if setup.inflation.baileyRelentless() and setup.inflation.percent(setup.inflation.baileyWealth()) lt 1>>
			/* Relentless toggle, but the player isn't actually rich: Bailey is squeezing for its own sake. */
			Bailey looks you up and down, then a slow, mean smile spreads across <<his>> face. <<He>> taps at <<his>> phone.
			"Here's how it's going to be. Doesn't matter how little you've got. My rent goes up, week after week, and you'll find a way to pay it."
			<br><br>
			<<His>> smile sharpens. "Consider it motivation. The more it hurts, the harder you'll work for me. I'll be wanting more every single week from now on."
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			Bailey looks you up and down, then a smirk spreads across <<his>> face. <<He>> taps at <<his>> phone.
			"Funny thing. Word gets around. Seems you've been sitting on quite the little fortune, haven't you? Holding out on me this whole time."
			<br><br>
			<<His>> smile sharpens. "Prices are going up for everyone, and your rent's no different. Only fair I get my share of what you've squirrelled away.
			I'll be wanting more from now on, and more again the fatter that purse of yours gets."
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "loanRentNotice">>
	/* One-time heads-up when an ignored HBSC loan first gets handed to Bailey to collect. */
	<<if setup.hbsc and setup.hbsc.ensureLoanState>>
		<<run setup.hbsc.ensureLoanState()>>
		<<if $hbsc.loan.baileyAnnouncePending>>
			<<set $hbsc.loan.baileyAnnouncePending to false>>
			"<span class="red">Before we settle up,</span>" Bailey says, "the bank's been in touch.
			You never paid back what you borrowed, so they've asked me to collect for them. From now on,
			part of what you hand me goes straight to clearing that debt. Lucky you."
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "homeeventtemplecharity">>
	<<generateTemple 1>><<generateyTemple 2>><<npc Bailey 3>>
	A <<person1>><<monk>> from the temple enters the orphanage, followed by several initiates carrying crates and a locked tin.
	Some of the orphans recognise the crates from the soup kitchen, and start whispering.
	<br><br>
	<<person3>>
	Bailey appears before the visitors can reach the stairs. <<He>> frowns at the tin.
	"If this is about the kitchen, take it upstairs and don't get in my way."
	<br><br>
	<<person1>>
	"It's more than food this time," the <<monk>> says. "People have been generous.
	We thought the residents should benefit directly."
	<br><br>
	<<person3>>
	"They benefit by having a roof," Bailey says. "And a roof costs money."
	<br><br>
	<<person1>>
	"This is charity," the <<monk>> replies. "It was given for the orphans."
	<br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Orphanage Charity Mod]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</widget>>

<<widget "shackleLockpick">>
	/* Shackles are a locksmith's job: the Lockpick Lawyer set plus SSS skulduggery is enough to do it yourself, in private, instead of paying the museum or the police. */
	<<if $worn.feet.type.includes("shackle") and $worn.feet.name isnot "vines" and !$possessed>>
		<<if $lockpickTrainingSet gte 5 and $skulduggery gte 2000>>
			<br>
			<<lockicon "pick">><<link [[Pick your shackles open with your Lockpick Lawyer set (0:20)|Bedroom Shackle Pick]]>><<pass 20>><</link>> | <span class="lustful">Skulduggery: SSS Mastery</span>
		<<elseif $lockpickTrainingSet gte 5 and !$settings.blindStatsEnabled>>
			<br>
			<span class="red">Pick your shackles open with your Lockpick Lawyer set</span> | <span class="lustful">Skulduggery: SSS Mastery required</span>
		<<elseif $skulduggery gte 2000 and !$settings.blindStatsEnabled>>
			<br>
			<span class="red">Pick your shackles open</span> | <span class="blue">The Lockpick Lawyer set required</span>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>
